# What `docker build` (context `.`) must NOT ship to the daemon. Every image installs its own
# dependencies and runs its own build, so anything generated locally is dead weight — and on a
# developer machine `apps/native/src-tauri/target` alone is several gigabytes.
# Nothing tracked in git matches these patterns; check that before adding one.

.git
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Secrets never belong in an image layer (compose passes the values as environment variables).
# The `**/` patterns are the ones that matter: `apps/api/` and `packages/` are copied into the api
# image's *runtime* stage and `apps/web/` into the web image's build stage, so a developer's
# `apps/api/.env` or `apps/web/.env.production` would otherwise be published with the image. The
# bare `.env` lines cover the repository root, which the `**/` forms do not match.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

# Rust build artifacts of the Tauri shells (the images do not build them)
apps/native/src-tauri/target
apps/native/src-tauri/gen

# Build output — every Dockerfile rebuilds what it needs inside the image
**/dist
**/build
**/.svelte-kit
**/.astro
**/.turbo
**/.wrangler

# Uploaded documents and backups from a local run
apps/api/data
data
backups

# Python
**/.venv
**/__pycache__

# Test artifacts
**/test-results
**/playwright-report

# Maintainer working notes, not part of the kit
HANDOFF.md
ROADMAP.md
